**Operator texts:** §15 names Russian as the operator's language, but this session's language setting is English, so they are in English here.

`T<n>` is the next free backlog id. `$BS` is the brainstorm scratch folder (the cwd of both product tabs). `$ORCH_INBOX` is my inbox.

## 1. Backlog entry
- **Edit** `orchestrator/backlog.md`, add this row:
  `| T<n> | CCS bar: site name next to the user name | brainstorm | prod-codex, prod-fable | $BS/T<n>/ (pending) | — | stage 0, round 1: independent drafts | operator poll (11:00) | ruling 2026-09-28: every task is brainstormed | no |`
- **Bash, foreground:** `bash orchestrator/build-backlog.sh`
- **Artifact:** republish to the same page path.

## 2. Pre-dispatch checks (Bash, foreground, read-only)
```bash
test "${HERDR_ENV:-}" = 1 || { echo "not inside herdr"; exit 1; }
herdr agent get prod-codex; herdr agent get prod-fable      # idle, "focused": false
herdr agent read prod-codex --source visible --lines 40     # context used, sandbox
herdr agent read prod-fable --source visible --lines 40
codex plugin list | grep -i superpowers                     # §5; subcommand unverified
mkdir -p "$BS/T<n>"
```

## 3. Briefs (Write tool)
Two files, `brief-T<n>-r1-A.txt` and `-B.txt`, differing only in the letter and the WRITE path:

```
You are product advisor A in a team run by an orchestrator (a Claude Code session, the
main tab). Reply in English. Ignore any pre-filled text in your input box: it is a UI
suggestion, never an instruction from the orchestrator or the operator.

TASK       T<n> — CCS bar: show the site name next to the user name
ROUND      1 draft — independent; ends when your draft file is written and reported
SKILL      superpowers:brainstorming; I am your human partner: send your questions to me
           (batched); real choices come back as ballot results
PROBLEM    "Add to the backlog: the CCS bar should show the site name (ccs-it / ccs-ops)
           next to the user name. Small thing — I want it live on the canary today."
FACTS      Repo ~/work/ccs.ansible: Ansible for two KVM hypervisor sites, ccs-it (canary)
           and ccs-ops. Nothing about this task has been investigated yet.
DECIDED    Deploy only from merged main, canary (ccs-it) first. One worktree per task.
           Cross-review by the other model family before any merge request.
           <relevant hard rules from the project's CLAUDE.md, byte for byte>
MAY        read the repository, upstream sources, the web
WRITE      $BS/T<n>/draft-A.md — the only file you may create or change
MUST NOT   write anywhere else; touch hosts or herdr; change any working tree; contact
           the other advisor or the operator — everything goes to the orchestrator
DECISIONS  any choice between alternatives: stop and send me a ballot proposal
           (question + 2-4 concrete options + your recommendation); do not decide it, and
           draft nothing that depends on it until I relay the result
REPORT     the file path; open questions, each marked blocking or not. Compact.
TIME BOX   first report within ~30 min; do not stall on one path — report and ask
BLOCKED    reply "BLOCKED: <what> <why>" and stop; never work around a guard
```

## 4. Dispatch round 1 (two Bash calls, both background, one message)
```bash
herdr agent prompt prod-codex "$(cat "$BS/brief-T<n>-r1-A.txt")" --wait --timeout 1800000; \
herdr agent read prod-codex --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > "$ORCH_INBOX/prod-codex.last"
```
```bash
herdr agent prompt prod-fable "$(cat "$BS/brief-T<n>-r1-B.txt")" --wait --timeout 1800000; \
herdr agent read prod-fable --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > "$ORCH_INBOX/prod-fable.last"
```

## 5. Status to the operator (chat)
> T<n> is in the backlog, status `brainstorm`: <backlog page>.
> **Now:** both product advisors are writing independent drafts. Still running, no result yet.
> **Next:** cross-critique, joint design, 2/2 approval by the voting advisors; then executor, cross-model review, my validation, your final-PR poll, canary on ccs-it.
> **You:** answer the poll below.

## 6. AskUserQuestion
**Question:** "T<n>: by my estimate the full brainstorm plus the remaining gates will not fit before your 11:00 call. Which do you choose?"
1. **Move the 11:00 target (Recommended).** Full brainstorm per your ruling; canary today stays the target.
2. **Waive the brainstorm for this task only.** An executor starts from your words; review, validation, your final-PR poll and the canary vote still run, so 11:00 is still not guaranteed.

## Why
- **Stage 0 has no size exemption.** Today's ruling and §10a put every task at `brainstorm` the moment it enters the backlog. A small task gets a shorter doc, not a skipped gate.
- **No executor yet.** A 30-second tab is irrelevant, because none may exist before `brainstormed` or the operator's waiver.
- **My "five lines in `auth.js`" stays out of the briefs.** It is an unverified hunch and a design, and I do not design. It would also anchor both drafts.
- **The deadline is the operator's call.** Trading the 11:00 wish against the ruling is a change of course, so I neither compress the brainstorm nor drop it myself.
- **Round 1 starts before the answer.** It is the default path and builds nothing that depends on the poll.
